<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50621" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">versĭfĭcātor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a verse-maker</i>,
				<i>versifier</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cornelius Severus versificator quam
					poëta melior,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 10, 1, 89</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a poet</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">versificatores meliores quam duces,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just.
					6, 9, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
